  "sources": {
    "reference": "NDS 2018: reference design values in psi (NDS Supplement Tables 4A, 4D, 5A); CD Table 2.3.2 (permanent 0.9, ten years 1.0, two months 1.15, seven days 1.25, ten minutes 1.6, impact 2.0); CM of dimension lumber Fb 0.85 (1.0 when Fb CF <= 1150 psi), Fv 0.97, Fc⊥ 0.67, Fc 0.8 (1.0 when Fc CF <= 750 psi), E 0.9; timbers Fc⊥ 0.67, Fc 0.91; glulam Fb 0.8, Ft 0.8, Fv 0.875, Fc⊥ 0.53, Fc 0.73, E 0.833; Ct Table 2.3.3; Ci Table 4.3.8; CF and Cfu Table 4A footnotes; timbers CF = (12/d)^(1/9); CV = (21/L)^(1/x) (12/d)^(1/x) (5.125/b)^(1/x), x = 10; Cr 1.15; CL Sec 3.3.3 with le of Table 3.3.3 (the 'any loading' row), RB <= 50, FbE = 1.20 Emin'/RB²; CP Sec 3.7.1, c 0.8 sawn, 0.9 glulam, FcE = 0.822 Emin'/(le/d)², le/d <= 50; Cb = (lb + 0.375)/lb under 6 in.; Appendix N: KF Fb 2.54, Ft 2.70, Fv 2.88, Fc 2.40, Fc⊥ 1.67, Emin 1.76, connections 3.32; φ 0.85, 0.80, 0.75, 0.90, 0.90, 0.85, connections 0.65; λ 0.6 (dead), 0.7 / 0.8 / 1.25 (storage / occupancy / impact live), 0.8 (roof live, snow), 1.0 (wind, earthquake); Chapter 12: Fe∥ = 11200 G, Fe⊥ = 6100 G^1.45 / √D (D >= 1/4 in.), 16600 G^1.84 (D < 1/4 in.), Rd 4 Kθ, 3.6 Kθ, 3.2 Kθ (Kθ = 1 + 0.25 θ/90), KD 2.2 (D <= 0.17 in.), 10 D + 0.5; Fyb 45 ksi bolts, nails by diameter; Cg Sec 11.3.6 (γ = 180 000 D^1.5); CΔ Table 12.5.1A, B; CM of fasteners in wet service 0.7 (Table 11.3.3)",
    "durationCases": "SAEngine practice: the load case names to durations (D, SD, F, H, T permanent; L the material's live load duration; Lr and R seven days; S two months; W, E and the flood load ten minutes); a live load named 'continuous' (the default) takes ten years (occupancy), λ 0.8",
    "location": "SAEngine practice: a material 'wet' or 'outside' is in wet service (moisture content above 19 %, NDS Sec 4.1.4)",
    "lengths": "SAEngine practice: le of columns is the member length (pinned ends, Ke = 1.0), lu of beams the type's restraint spacing (else the length); side members of bolted and nailed joints of the member's species, as deep as the member"
  }
}
